# Words after a lone year marker that open the next clause, so the marker
# closes the year phrase before them. Subject pronouns. Source: Huddleston
# and Pullum, The Cambridge Grammar of the English Language (2002), the
# chapter on personal pronouns. English puts its year marker before the month
# ("last january") or reads a year phrase ("january last year"), so the list
# is kept for parity with the other locales.
i
we
you
he
she
they
it
